s in no particular order, and a Score’s levels are ordered, so each formula below builds on the one before it.`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`TypeSafe’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`confidence`}),` is one reasonable way to summarize a distribution, not the only one. We return a fixed measure so that every answer comes with a sensible default: you can gate on `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`confidence`}),` from your first call, on the same 0 to 1 scale for every question, without first choosing and validating a statistic of your own. Because the formulas below are exact and every answer includes its full `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`probabilities`}),`, you can compute whichever measure matters most to your application instead.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`noul`,children:`Noul`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A Noul answer is a single probability `,_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`katex`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`katex-mathml`,children:_jsx(_components.math,{xmlns:`http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML`,children:_jsxs(_components.semantics,{children:[_jsx(_components.mrow,{children:_jsx(_components.mi,{children:`p`})}),_jsx(_components.annotation,{encoding:`application/x-tex`,children:`p`})]})})}),_jsx(_components.span,{className:`katex-html`,\"aria-hidden\":`true`,children:_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`base`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`strut`,style:{height:`0.625em`,verticalAlign:`-0.1944em`}}),_jsx(_components.span,{className:`mord mathnormal`,children:`p`})]})})]}),` that the answer is yes, and TypeSafe returns no separate `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`confidence`}),` for it. The probability already carries the uncertainty: a value near 0.5 is the model saying it is unsure, and the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/primitives/noul`,children:`Noul`}),` page covers how to threshold on it directly.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`If you want a confidence-style number anyway, for exampl